{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1301299-m20-entropy-and-other-spheres","id":1301299,"title":"M20 Entropy and other Spheres","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-31T07:07:33-07:00","id":1301299,"title":"M20 Entropy and other Spheres","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> A list of a few sphere questions that keep popping up in my group: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Entropy 1 allows the mage to &quot;<i>spot weak spots in objects, people, or arguments</i>&quot;. Does this effect require Matter, Life or Mind respectively or it is a property of Entropy on its own? The Matter 1 write up describes &quot;<i> ...when combining this perception with Entropy \u2013 spot <b>[an object]</b> weak points</i>&quot;, implying that Matter needs Entropy, but Entropy does not require Matter for that effect.</li> <li>Data (Correspondence) does not work without internet/radio signals? In a post-apocalyptic scenario, all Data (Correspondence) ranks become useless?</li> <li>Data (Correspondence) write-up states &quot;<i>To use Data-based Effects, the technomancer must collate data about the person or location he\u2019s trying to reach, <b>and then have gear in place that can reach the subject </b>of his attention.</i>&quot; The gear has to be technomancy, or can it be regular technology like a tv-set, cellphone, computer, camera, etc?</li> </ol><br /> <br /> Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 03-31-2019, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T23:00:16-07:00","id":1301527,"title":"","content":"I think...Re: point one - I found a write-up that had this line in Entropy 1: &quot;Combined with various Pattern Spheres, the mage can look for weaknesses in a Pattern or see where it will fracture naturally.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think it depends on your game. How I would likely run it is that, with just Entropy, you get a sense that there is some weakness or inherent chaos involved, but maybe not specifically. But, by combining with other spheres, you build on that sense to specificity with that Pattern type. For example, with Entropy 1, I may detect as I walk down the street that there is a bit of weakness somewhere nearby, but not pinpoint it beyond a general area or possibly direction. I know a weakness is close, but I can't necessarily tell what it is or with what. Some triangulation may help narrow down the weakened object, but not specify the weakness. But, by having other spheres, I get a sense of what is weak and in what way. If the weakness was a person's will to resist cheating on their diet at the coffee shop, Mind will pick that up. Someone on the verge of a heart attack will pop up with Life. And so on.<br /> <br /> Re: 2) - That is my read on it. You may be able to use it if you find some old tech and get it working again, but only to analyze the data on that device. However, with Forces, you may be able to provide the energy to some form of infrastructure to get just enough of a signal to utilize data... it'd be tricky and risk Paradox, but you COULD possibly do it if the infrastructure existed (i.e. underground telecom lines that may have survived the disaster may work as a medium; you put forces into the network to scope it out and create a signal along those paths.<br /> <br /> 3. So I think the confusion is in terms. All magic that uses technology as the tool is, in some sense, technomantic. I think you may have been thinking &quot;Technocratic&quot; - as in, the advanced tech they keep to themselves because the masses don't accept it yet. If that is your meaning (and if not then I apologize for misunderstanding), the answer is no, it doesn't have to be. As long as it fits your practices and can provide a connection to that target, you could use perfectly mundane technology to work data against a subject you have information about. In fact, it's arguably built on the idea that you are using regular tech, since hypertech would risk Paradox. A Data-using Technocrat (or VA member even) just needs to have a way to get info on the person remotely and then a way to get a hold of them or their general area. CCTV, cell phones, webcams, and so on all work just as well as channels for Data practices as the prototype of the iPhone XX Iteration X just designed that hasn't been released because it incorporates holotech that is about ten generations of phone away from being acceptable to the Consensus. That requirement is less about the means and more about the availability - if your target is in the woods with no tech and no one nearby, you can't use data to reach them because they don't have a connection. The best case scenario would be accessing a spy or mapping satellite (legitimately or otherwise) and getting their position with the cameras as a form of spying, but you still wouldn't be able to go there through the Data sphere since there isn't a direct connection to follow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T00:29:47-07:00","id":1301543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1301299-m20-entropy-and-other-spheres#post1301299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings,<br /> <br /> A list of a few sphere questions that keep popping up in my group:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Entropy 1 allows the mage to &quot;<i>spot weak spots in objects, people, or arguments</i>&quot;. Does this effect require Matter, Life or Mind respectively or it is a property of Entropy on its own? The Matter 1 write up describes &quot;<i> ...when combining this perception with Entropy \u2013 spot <b>[an object]</b> weak points</i>&quot;, implying that Matter needs Entropy, but Entropy does not require Matter for that effect.</li> <li>Data (Correspondence) does not work without internet/radio signals? In a post-apocalyptic scenario, all Data (Correspondence) ranks become useless?</li> <li>Data (Correspondence) write-up states &quot;<i>To use Data-based Effects, the technomancer must collate data about the person or location he\u2019s trying to reach, <b>and then have gear in place that can reach the subject </b>of his attention.</i>&quot; The gear has to be technomancy, or can it be regular technology like a tv-set, cellphone, computer, camera, etc?</li> </ol><br /> <br /> Thanks,</div> </div> </div> </div>1: I'd say that Entropy 1 allows you to sense the weaknesses in abstract things, like ideas. You can use Entropy 1 to tell if something is a lie, or to find the weakness in an argument or concept. Entropy 1 is also allowing you to see if someone is important to your destiny (assuming you believe that you can measure that sort of thing; Black Suit's don't go in for horoscope bullshit). But yes, if you want to see the weakness in a person's body (their crippling heart disease and fatty alcoholic liver), or the weakness in a building (how a load-baring wall has been weakened by damp and rot), then you need to add the relevant Spheres. You can get very creative with this though; see how someone's mind is weak with Mind 1 Entropy 1, and try and get an impression of what mental illnesses or frailties they have, and how you could exploit them.<br /> <br /> 2: The Data Sphere demands that the target be linked to the digital world somehow, and makes it very hard to use magick on people who are COMPLETELY off the grid. Very hard isn't quite the same as impossible, since anyone with the Data Sphere will realize that all reality is data regardless, and can find a workaround (which is working without focus, so +3 difficulty unless you're practically and archmage).<br /> <br /> As for a post-apocalypse scenario, if the Mage set up their own security system, local radio and data network / intranet, that would make the Data sphere useful again. Easy for a Data-using Mage since they have all the right skills/knowledges, and their Spheres reduce difficulties. Even a smart sleeper could do all that. Data 1 also allows a Mage to see directions and distances in the same way Correspondence 1 does, worth remembering. But yes if you threw a VA into the Dark Ages they'd struggle.<br /> <br /> 3: You can work via regular tech. So for example, if you did extensive searches for a character via the internet, and finally found them with your Data senses (Scrying, essentially), you'd be able to target the security system around him (with the right magick, or the right hacking rolls) to do something like lock him in the elevator he's in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}